INT. AUCTION HOUSE, ANTIQUE CLOCK VIEWING ROOM - EVENING

A hundred clocks tick in conflict. Brass, ormolu, walnut, lacquer. Velvet ropes. A single white-gloved attendant by the door.

CELESTINE VOSS, 40s, in a grey silk dress that costs more than the carpet, drifts between cases with a catalogue folded under her arm, while RHYS, 30s, dressed as a waiter with a tray of champagne flutes, steps between two bidders without spilling, and OKSANA, 50s, an appraiser in half-moon glasses, peers into the open back of a bracket clock, and Celestine pauses, tilts her head toward the clock Oksana is examining, and Oksana, without lifting her eyes, shifts a half-step to give her a clearer view.

PEMBERTON, 60s, the auctioneer, pink-faced, approaches Celestine with a practiced smile.

PEMBERTON
Madam Voss. A pleasure. You've found the Thwaites.

CELESTINE
It found me.

PEMBERTON
Estimated at forty thousand.

CELESTINE
It's worth less.

PEMBERTON
Less?

CELESTINE
It's missing its pendulum.

Pemberton blinks. Oksana's pencil pauses. Rhys sets the tray on a plinth without looking at it.

PEMBERTON
The pendulum was lost in the war.

CELESTINE
I'm sure it was.

She moves on. Pemberton follows a half-step behind. Rhys lifts a flute, offers it. She takes it, drinks nothing, sets it down on the velvet rope.

THADDEUS, 20s, the white-gloved attendant, steps forward to retrieve it. Celestine smiles at him as one smiles at a stranger on a train, and he retreats.

At the far end of the room, Oksana draws a hair-thin wire from her sleeve and slips it behind the clock's dial, so smoothly that Pemberton, glancing back at her, sees only a woman adjusting her glasses.

PEMBERTON
Oksana, you're quiet.

OKSANA
I'm counting.

PEMBERTON
Counting what?

OKSANA
Seconds.

Pemberton laughs. Celestine does not. Her eyes, for a moment, meet Rhys's across the room.

The hundred clocks begin to chime the hour, in no particular order, and in the roar of it, Thaddeus, tugging his gloves, sees the Thwaites case swing open an inch.

THADDEUS
Sir? Sir, the case --

PEMBERTON
(over the chimes)
What?

THADDEUS
The case --

CELESTINE
(sweetly)
Have a glass of champagne, young man.

Rhys appears at his elbow. Thaddeus takes the flute. Drinks. The case stays open.
